Z||000000||sqoach||11-24-2000||07:35 PM||||man, i swear i have the most problems with a car.  when i take a rather sharp turn, my wheels or something is making a clattering noise.  and when i'm turning to go in my driveway (it's a small incline) it's a little more noticeable.  i don't think it's hurting anything, but it's really annoying.  i've checked my bearings and they're ok.  i don't know what to check.  any answers to this one?  thanks.<P>------------------<BR>sQoaCh||||reg||11
Z||000001||theogre||11-24-2000||07:42 PM||||look for contact marks on the stone shields where the brake rotors have hit them. You probably have one a little bent. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Omnipotence||11-28-2000||07:21 PM||||had the same problem on my 90 Grandam check the balljoints||||reg||3
Z||000003||Indiana_resto_guy||11-28-2000||10:48 PM||||Don't overlook the CV joints. If you have a broken boot, chances are good for a bad one.||||reg||1
